    "title": "pandas.MultiIndex.dtypes — pandas 3.1.0.dev0+1662.g0c49719283 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.MultiIndex.dtypes#\n\n- MultiIndex.dtypes[source]#\n- Return the dtypes as a Series for the underlying MultiIndex. Each element in the returned Series corresponds to the dtype of one level of the MultiIndex, indexed by the level names. See also \n  - `Index.dtype`\n  - Return the dtype object of the underlying data.\n  - `Series.dtypes`\n  - Return the data type of the underlying Series.\n Examples >>> idx = pd.MultiIndex.from_product( ... [(0, 1, 2), (\"green\", \"purple\")], names=[\"number\", \"color\"] ... ) >>> idx MultiIndex([(0, 'green'), (0, 'purple'), (1, 'green'), (1, 'purple'), (2, 'green'), (2, 'purple')], names=['number', 'color']) >>> idx.dtypes number int64 color object dtype: object",
    "markdown_length": 700,
